{"name":"Goose Pond Green","hex":"#629b92","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"goose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various grazing waterfowl of the family Anatidae, which have feathers and webbed feet and are capable of flying, swimming, and walking on land, and which are generally bigger than ducks.","A female goose."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sharply poke or pinch the buttocks, or prod between the buttocks (of a person).","To stimulate; to spur."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goose"},{"term":"pond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inland body of standing water, either natural or man-made, that is smaller than a lake.","An inland body of standing water of any size that is fed by springs rather than by a river."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Chiefly in across the pond: the Atlantic Ocean."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pond"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goose","blocks":[{"text":"A goose is a bird of any of several waterfowl species in the family Anatidae. This group comprises the genera Anser and Branta. Some members of the Tadorninae subfamily are commonly called geese, but are not considered \"true geese\" taxonomically. More distantly related members of the family Anatidae are swans, most of which are larger than true geese, and ducks, which are smaller."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goose","wikidata":"Q16529344"},{"title":"Pond","blocks":[{"text":"A pond is a small, still, land-based body of water formed by pooling inside a depression, either naturally or artificially. A pond is smaller than a lake and there are no official criteria distinguishing the two, although defining a pond to be less than 5 hectares in area, less than 5 metres (16 ft) in depth and with less than 30% of its area covered by emergent vegetation helps in distinguishing the ecology of ponds from those of lakes and wetlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg/330px-Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pond","wikidata":"Q12719646"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/500px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/1280px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/500px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Snow geese (Anser caerulescens) in Quebec, Canada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG/500px-B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG/1280px-B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG/500px-B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chinese geese (Anser cygnoides domesticus), the domesticated form of the swan goose (Anser cygnoides)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AB%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Geese_in_Naantali%2C_Finland.jpg/500px-Geese_in_Naantali%2C_Finland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe